cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Explicit peak demand representation in least-cost electrification
  modelling: evidence from Zambia
message: If you use this model or its results, please cite the paper.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Eladia
    family-names: Alcoverro Gea
    affiliation: Department of Chemical Engineering, Imperial College London
repository-code: https://github.com/zceceal/zambia-explicit-peak
abstract: >-
  A controlled two-configuration OnSSET experiment testing whether replacing
  the uniform load-factor convention with an explicit, settlement-specific
  peak power changes least-cost electrification outcomes across 270,526
  Zambian settlements.
keywords:
  - electrification
  - OnSSET
  - peak demand
  - least-cost planning
  - Zambia
